st about  one third to one half of the way up this  helps cook your cheesecake more evenly  and also it's gonna keep it from forming  a dome and cracking so we're gonna put  this in the oven on 300 for about two  hours and then once it's all cooked  through you're gonna put it in the  refrigerator overnight and you need that  full chill all the way through so you  can slice it perfectly and it sets  really nicely okay so now we're gonna  make candy pecans i like to do this on  the first day that way you can get it  out the way let it cool and set ready  for day two and you can put it as your  topping we've got our  water here  we've got our sugar  and we've got some corn syrup  this is on a medium-high heat you don't  want it too hot because you don't want  to cook your sugar too fast you want to  cook your sugar for about three to five  minutes once you get a nice glossy color  you can add your pecans this time you  really want to stir this constantly make  sure you kind of keep them separated so  they don't stick together too much once  your pecans are nice and coated and  glossy we're gonna take  a parchment lined pan and you're just  gonna pour it right on the sheet  be sure to separate your pecans out  while they set take your cheesecake out  of the oven put it in the refrigerator  and then take a nap you deserve it we'll  come back on day two and finish off our  cheesecake  all right so it's day two i've removed  the cheesecake from the foil and the  water bath it's nice and set and you're  just gonna pop it open right from the  bottom it should come right out we have  melted our chocolate and we've also just  reheated our caramel from yesterday  first you're going to drizzle the  chocolate you want to do like a zigzag  and you want to make sure that the  consistency  is liquidy but also thick so it holds  you add your pecans it looks so crunchy  so crispy i'm going to use all of these  there's no such thing as too many pecans  and then once you've chopped it 